TY  - JOUR
TI  - Intractable sneezing with a specific psychogenic origin
PY  - 1986
JO  - Annals of Allergy
AB  - A case of intractable sneezing due to a specific psychogenic cause is described. Identification of the cause led to resolution of the symptoms which had not otherwise responded to maximum pharmacologic intervention. The current patient underwent a thorough history, physical examination, skin-testing, sinus x-rays, environmental control, and a trial of numerous medications. It was the atypical features of the sneezing such as lack of symptoms during sleep, the association with multiple fainting episodes only in the presence of other people, negative objective test results, and lack of response to medications, that finally led to the consideration of a psychogenic cause and the subsequent revelation of the history of sexual abuse.
